# wasm-pack writes its bundle into this directory: the `.js` glue, the
# `.wasm` binary and the `.d.ts` bindings. All of that is generated, so it
# stays out of the repository.
*

# `package.json` is not wasm-pack output. It is hand-written source: it names
# the shim package, declares the license of record, and lists which generated
# files the package ships in `files`. It has to be versioned.
#
# It was previously swept up by the `*` above and never committed, so
# `test_package_json_declares_the_same_license` passed on any maintainer
# checkout that had run `wasm-pack build` and failed in CI, where the
# generated bundle does not exist and the file must come from git. A contract
# test that only passes when a build has been run locally is not a contract.
!package.json
